1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. d3 h6 5. f4 d6 6. Nf3 Bg4 7. O-O { h3 was good too } 7... exf4 (7... Nd4 8. fxe5 Bxf3 9. gxf3 dxe5 10. f4) 8. Bxf4 Nd4 { now is a very good time to open the centre with e5, but we have other moves } 9. Qd2 { just connecting our rooks } 9... Nxf3+ 10. gxf3 { The only good move! } 10... Be6 11. Kh1 Qd7 12. Qf2 { explain Qf2 } 12... Bxc4 13. dxc4 Qc6 14. b3 Be7 15. Rg1 Nh5 16. Be3 a6 17. Nd5 Bg5 18. f4 Bf6 19. Bd4 Bxd4 20. Qxd4 Rg8 21. Qd1 { Doubling rooks also good. What is Qd1 doing btw? } 21... Nf6 (21... Nxf4 22. Nxf4 Qxe4+ 23. Ng2) 22. Nxf6+ Ke7 23. Nxg8+ Rxg8 24. Qd5 *


