1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. d3 Bc5 5. f4 d6 6. Nf3 O-O { Unlike chapter 6, here they castle (second most common) instead of jumping in with Ng4. } { [%cal Gf4f5,Gc3a4] } 7. f5 Ng4? { 10%. Nd4 is played more. } 8. Bg5 { Best but Ng5 works too and wins a lot because 8... Nf2 is a huge blunder (we just play Qh5 and he has to sac pieces) however 8... Bf2+ is rare but annoying, we play Kf1, then he forks, we trade pieces, h4, black's Queen comes in... } (8. Ng5 Nf2 (8... Bf2+ 9. Kf1 Ne3+ 10. Bxe3 Bxe3 11. h4 Bxg5 12. hxg5 Qxg5) 9. Qh5) 8... Qe8 (8... Bf2+ 9. Kd2) 9. Nd5 Nf2 10. Qd2 Nxh1 11. Nf6+ gxf6 12. Bxf6 { Mate in 6! } *


